Z||000000||daveml66||03-10-2001||05:07 PM||||i've put a 4spd in my former auto car every thing is fine the clutch shifter every thing has power and the engine will start if you bypass the key.  the ignition switch works tho it worked fine b4. i did not change the wiring harness on the inside of car and some one told me the clutch/nuetral switch is my problem but i have no wiring for it how can it be a problem?  what can i do?  every thing works it just won't crank by key ......||||reg||9
Z||000001||Phil||03-10-2001||07:51 PM||||Correct you don't have clutch/neutral circuit but you do have a park/neutral circuit from the auto.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||03-10-2001||10:08 PM||||What did you do about the park-neutral switch?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Archie||03-10-2001||10:30 PM||||The quick solution is to find the gang plug that used to plug into your automatic transmission (near the selector lever) and connect the heavy gage Yellow & Purple Wires together.<P>Note: your car will start in gear with this modification, so don't forget to push in the clutch.<P>Many times people aho are used to automatic shift cars will forget to push in the clutch on a car that has just been converted to stick shift. Thus, IT IS HIGHLY RECOMMENDED that you install a stick shift style switch on the clutch pedal and run the Yellow & Purple wires to it.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000004||daved||03-10-2001||10:47 PM||||You will have to install a "clutch/start switch" for the clutch pedal, and connect it to the Yellow wire coming from the ignition switch.  The other side of the "clutch/start switch" will be a purple wire connected to the S terminal on the starter.  You will have to supply this wire (you could use any coloured wire though).  Dave ||||reg||1
Z||000005||daveml66||03-13-2001||09:31 AM||||i wanted to thank u guys for the replies. my 87gt starts and runs great as a 4spd. i just completely bypassed the clutch switch. i'm used to driving a standard neway. i had just bought this car because it had a bad engine and i had exactaly what it needed<BR>thanks.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by daveml66 (edited 03-13-2001).]||||reg||6
